---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Methodology · vegastack-cli evals"
  description="How the vegastack-cli public eval dashboard is computed: lift formula, baseline-vs-skill methodology, expectation kinds."
>
  <article class="container-prose py-16 md:py-24 max-w-3xl">
    <p class="mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-subtle">Methodology</p>
    <h1
      class="display-num text-[clamp(2.25rem,5vw,3.5rem)] font-medium mt-4 reveal"
    >
      How we measure lift.
    </h1>

    <p class="text-muted text-lg mt-6 leading-relaxed reveal reveal-delay-1">
      Every claim on this site reduces to one number: the fraction of the
      remaining error that the skill closes versus a clean baseline run of
      the same model on the same prompt with the same scoring.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-12 reveal reveal-delay-2">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight">The lift formula</h2>
      <pre
        class="surface-card mono text-sm p-5 mt-4 overflow-x-auto"
        style="color: var(--fg-default);"
      >
lift = (with_skill_pass_rate - baseline_pass_rate)
       / (1 - baseline_pass_rate)</pre>
      <p class="text-muted mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        A baseline that already passes 80% has only 20% of error left to
        close — closing 10pp more of total counts as 50% lift, not 10%.
        This formula keeps the headline meaningful as the model improves.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 reveal reveal-delay-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight">
        Baseline vs with-skill
      </h2>
      <ol class="mt-4 flex flex-col gap-4 text-muted leading-relaxed">
        <li>
          <span class="text-[color:var(--fg-default)] font-medium">Baseline.</span>
          The baseline model sees only the prompt — no <code class="mono text-sm">vegastack ask --entry terraform --tf-provider <provider></code>
          tool, no skill files, no Terraform-specific context.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="text-[color:var(--fg-default)] font-medium">With skill.</span>
          The same model + same prompt + the vegastack-cli skill mounted
          in the harness. The model decides when to call the
          <code class="mono text-sm">vegastack ask --entry terraform --tf-provider <provider></code> bash tool, reads the
          four-channel envelope, and writes its answer.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="text-[color:var(--fg-default)] font-medium">Scoring.</span>
          Each prompt has 3-7 hand-authored expectations. Each is graded
          independently by an LLM judge with a yes/no rubric. We run the
          judge three times and take the median to dampen variance.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 reveal reveal-delay-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight">Expectation kinds</h2>
      <p class="text-muted mt-3 leading-relaxed">
        Every expectation declares its kind so the judge prompt can be
        tightened — most are deterministic regex/AST checks, only a few
        are open-ended.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-2.5 mono text-sm">
        <li class="surface-card p-3">
          <span class="text-accent">resource_present</span>
          <span class="text-subtle"> — HCL contains the named resource</span>
        </li>
        <li class="surface-card p-3">
          <span class="text-accent">no_resource</span>
          <span class="text-subtle"> — catches hallucinated resource names</span>
        </li>
        <li class="surface-card p-3">
          <span class="text-accent">argument_present / argument_absent</span>
          <span class="text-subtle"> — validates a specific arg or its absence</span>
        </li>
        <li class="surface-card p-3">
          <span class="text-accent">import_syntax_match</span>
          <span class="text-subtle">
             — composite-ID format matches the manifest entry
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="surface-card p-3">
          <span class="text-accent">cites_card / cites_recipe / cites_path</span>
          <span class="text-subtle">
             — the skill surfaced the right knowledge artifact
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="surface-card p-3">
          <span class="text-accent">manifest_check</span>
          <span class="text-subtle">
             — a custom rule (e.g. "all required_args present")
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 reveal">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight">Why we publish failures</h2>
      <p class="text-muted mt-3 leading-relaxed">
        The public dashboard shows three failure exemplars from each run.
        Failed expectations directly drive next quarter's content authoring
        — if A12 lift drops, we audit the deprecation cards. If A5 lift
        drops, the soft-dep companion graph gets a review. Public failures
        are how we keep ourselves honest.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 reveal">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight">Honest caveats</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 flex flex-col gap-3 text-muted leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
        <li>
          The baseline is one model on one day. We don't claim general lift
          over every coding model — only over the specific baseline named
          in each run.
        </li>
        <li>
          LLM-judge scoring is noisy. Single-prompt deltas are meaningless;
          rolling 4-week medians are what we promote on.
        </li>
        <li>
          Prompts are author-curated to match the 12-archetype taxonomy.
          They are not a random sample from production traffic.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
